Principal diagnosis: massive hemoptysis, treated by bronchial artery embolization, in a patient who was SARS-CoV-2 positive. The choice is between R04 (hemorrhage from respiratory passages) and U07 (COVID-19).

The episode was admitted for hemoptysis and treated with embolization. Respiratory sampling was positive for COVID-19, but there was no pneumonia, and the hemoptysis was the focus of care. In ICD-10-AM the hemoptysis symptom code is R04. If COVID-19 were the cause of the bleeding, U07 might apply, but the case reads as hemoptysis being the reason for admission and the main treatment. I chose R04.

{"code": "R04", "condition": "Haemorrhage from respiratory passages (massive haemoptysis)"}
